+The slice is done: a server's program is now looked for in folder lists the window passes, then PATH, then home folders. All five acceptance items were observed. In the real app, oxlint, oxfmt and TypeScript started from `web/node_modules/.bin` as before, and none were left running after close.
+
+```
+summary
+  - lsp-host: `ProgramFolders { project, home }` replaces the fixed `BIN_FOLDER`. Search order: each `project` entry
+    (in list order) in the project folder and each parent up to the root, then PATH, then each `home` entry in the
+    home folder (`ProgramPlace::Home`). Entries that are not plain `/`-separated names are skipped.
+  - `ServerCommand.folders`; `Host::find_program(program, project, folders)`; `start` passes `command.folders`; the
+    Tauri `find_program` command takes `folders`.
+  - Window: `ProgramFolders` in ipc; `ServerHost.findProgram(program, project, folders)`; `ServerSpec.folders`;
+    one constant `PROGRAM_FOLDERS = { project: ["node_modules/.bin"], home: [] }` in lsp/internal/spec.ts, used by
+    detection's lookups, every detected spec and every added spec. The start command sends `spec.folders`.
+
+files_changed
+  crates/lsp-host/src/program.rs, crates/lsp-host/src/files.rs, crates/lsp-host/src/lib.rs,
+  crates/lsp-host/tests/run.rs, crates/lsp-host/tests/files.rs, crates/lsp-host/AGENTS.md,
+  src-tauri/src/servers.rs,
+  frontend/src/ipc/domain.ts, frontend/src/ipc/ServerHost.ts, frontend/src/ipc/index.ts, frontend/src/ipc/tauri.ts,
+  frontend/src/ipc/tauri.test.ts,
+  frontend/src/lsp/internal/spec.ts, detect.ts, added.ts, server.ts, frontend/src/lsp/AGENTS.md,
+  frontend/src/lsp/index.test.ts, frontend/src/lsp/internal/{added,attempt,detect,spec}.test.ts,
+  frontend/src/ui/{question,serverText,servers}.test.ts (spec literals only)
+  frontend/src/ipc/bindings.ts — GENERATED by `just bindings`, left in the tree (see deviations)
+
+tests_added (crates/lsp-host/src/program.rs unless noted)
+  two_project_entries_in_one_folder_are_tried_in_list_order — list order inside one folder; the nearer folder
+    wins over an earlier entry in a parent
+  nothing_above_the_root_is_searched — a program above the root is not found and that folder is not in `searched`
+  a_home_entry_is_found_after_path_with_place_home — found in home with place Home
+  path_beats_home — PATH comes before home
+  empty_absolute_and_dotted_entries_are_never_searched — "", "/abs", "a/../b", "./x", "a//b" in both lists: never
+    searched (decoys at project/b, project/x, home/b are not found) and not in `searched`
+  not_found_lists_every_folder_searched_in_order — 2 project entries × 3 folders, then 2 PATH entries, then 2 home entries
+  without_a_home_folder_home_entries_are_skipped — no home folder, so home entries are absent from `searched`
+  existing, kept and passing: the_project_s_own_bin_folder_wins_over_its_parents_and_path (nearest folder first),
+    a_parent_s_bin_folder_up_to_the_root_comes_before_path (PATH only after every project folder);
+    Windows PATHEXT tests left as they were
+  src-tauri servers.rs find_program_finds_a_project_s_program_and_project_files_reads_the_repository — the
+    command now takes `folders` as JSON
+  frontend lsp/index.test.ts "an added server's start command looks in node_modules/.bin like a detected one";
+    "rule 2: a spec starts…" now asserts `folders` on the start command
+  frontend lsp/internal/detect.test.ts — every `findProgram` call carries { project: ["node_modules/.bin"], home: [] };
+    detected specs carry it
+  frontend ipc/tauri.test.ts — `start` and `findProgram` pass `folders` through to the commands
+
+smoke_evidence
+  1. cargo test -p yamt-lsp-host -p yamt-app
+       test program::tests::two_project_entries_in_one_folder_are_tried_in_list_order ... ok
+       test program::tests::nothing_above_the_root_is_searched ... ok
