+     cargo fmt --all --check → FMT_OK
+  3. just bindings → frontend/src/ipc/bindings.ts:
+       31: findProgram: (program: string, project: string, folders: ProgramFolders) => __TAURI_INVOKE<ProgramFound>("find_program", { program, project, folders }),
+       218: export type ProgramFolders = {  220: project: string[],  222: home: string[],  };
+       227: export type ProgramPlace = "Project" | "Path" | "Home";
+       ServerCommand: 243: project: string,  244: folders: ProgramFolders,
+     domain.ts: `ProgramFolders = Readonly<Record<keyof Generated.ProgramFolders, readonly string[]>>` (the same keys,
+     project and home, as readonly string arrays); ServerCommand gains `readonly folders: ProgramFolders`;
+     ServerHost.ts: `findProgram(program: string, project: string, folders: ProgramFolders): Promise<ProgramFound>`.
+  4. pnpm -C frontend lint → `oxlint --type-aware && eslint …` exit 0; typecheck → `vue-tsc -b` exit 0;
+     test → Test Files 96 passed (96), Tests 1216 passed (1216); unused → `knip --include exports,types` exit 0;
+     fmt:check → "All matched files use the correct format." (whole chain EXIT=0)
+  5. Real app: XDG_CONFIG_HOME/XDG_DATA_HOME=/tmp/yamt-test-lsp-presetsfolders-xdg/… scripts/lsp-repo.sh --servers
+     /tmp/yamt-test-lsp-presetsfolders; built with `cargo tauri build --debug --no-bundle`; run through
+     `app-session start-app` (private Xvfb, private HOME and XDG_CONFIG_HOME). Answered Start, opened web/src/math.ts.
+     Logs:
+       "oxlint log / 11:59:52 / yamt / Starting oxlint --lsp in web"
+       "oxfmt log / 11:59:52 / yamt / Starting oxfmt --lsp in web"
+       "TypeScript log / 11:59:52 / yamt / Starting typescript-language-server --stdio in web"
+       menus: "oxlint Running …", "oxfmt Running …", "TypeScript Running …"
+     The start line names the program but not its folder (that is how the log line already was). So the path was
+     checked separately: find_program through the window's invoke →
+       {"path":"/tmp/yamt-test-lsp-presetsfolders/web/node_modules/.bin/oxlint","place":"Project"},
+       {"path":"…/web/node_modules/.bin/oxfmt","place":"Project"},
+       {"path":"…/web/node_modules/.bin/typescript-language-server","place":"Project"}
+     Children of `target/debug/yamt --repo /tmp/yamt-test-lsp-presetsfolders` (pid 238233):
+       238938 node /tmp/yamt-test-lsp-presetsfolders/web/node_modules/.bin/typescript-language-server --stdio
+       238925 / 238931 node …/frontend/node_modules/.bin/../oxfmt|oxlint/bin/… --lsp (the web/.bin links lead into frontend/)
+     After `app-session stop --name pf`:
+       pgrep -af 'oxlint|oxfmt|typescript-language-server' →
+         5711 …/home/wds/Projects/yamt/frontend/node_modules/.bin/../oxlint/bin/oxlint --lsp
+         5718 …/home/wds/Projects/yamt/frontend/node_modules/.bin/../oxfmt/bin/oxfmt --lsp
+       Both were already running before the app started (the owner's own editor, not this tree); pids
+       238925/238931/238938 are gone. pgrep for target/debug/yamt → NONE.
+
+deviations_from_brief
+  - The contract's doc comment on `ProgramFolders` changed its examples from "…" quotes to `…` backticks;
+    clippy::doc_markdown (-D warnings) rejects `node_modules/.bin` without them. No signature changed.
+  - domain.ts: `ProgramFolders` is written as `Readonly<Record<keyof Generated.ProgramFolders, readonly string[]>>`
+    (the same type as the brief's literal, keys tied to the generated type) with no blank line before
+    `ServerCommand`. eslint max-lines (300) failed at 301 with the literal form; the file is now exactly 300 lines.
+  - files.rs: the plain-name check was pulled out of `in_repository` into `plain_name` and reused by program.rs
+    (the brief's "reuse files.rs's rule"); `in_repository` behaves as before.
+  - The test-only environment input is a private `Environment { path_variable, home }` struct in program.rs, in
+    place of more `find_with_path` arguments.
+  - frontend/src/ipc/bindings.ts is changed in the tree by `just bindings`. Restoring it would need a git write
+    command, which SP9 forbids. A fresh export by the orchestrator gives the same file.
+  - Files outside Owned that still describe the old lookup (exact text to change):
+      docs/architecture.md:367-368 `find_program(program, project) -> ProgramFound` (the project's `node_modules/.bin`, …)
+        → `find_program(program, project, folders: ProgramFolders) -> ProgramFound` (each `folders.project` entry in the
+          project and its parents up to the root, then PATH, then each `folders.home` entry in the home folder; `searched` in order)
+      .omp/skills/ipc-contract/SKILL.md:59 `find_program(program, project) -> ProgramFound   Found{path, place: Project | Path} | …: node_modules/.bin up to the root, then PATH`
+        → `find_program(program, project, folders) -> ProgramFound   Found{path, place: Project | Path | Home} | NotFound{searched}: folders.project up to the root, then PATH, then folders.home`
+      .omp/skills/project-map/SKILL.md:40 `program (lookup: the project's node_modules/.bin up to the root, then PATH;`
+        → `program (lookup: the window's ProgramFolders — project entries up to the root, then PATH, then home entries;`
+
+open_risks
+  - frontend/src/ipc/domain.ts is exactly 300 lines, the max-lines limit; the next addition there must split the file.
+  - crates/lsp-host/src/program.rs:59 `env::home_dir()` reads HOME on Unix. No home-folder entries are sent yet, so
+    today's behaviour does not depend on it. RS17 ("env reads carry #[expect]") is not applied, matching the existing
+    `env::var_os("PATH")` next to it, and clippy reports no disallowed_methods.
+  - A home entry ending in `/` ("go/bin/") is skipped as "not plain names" (an empty segment). That follows the
+    brief's rule but could surprise whoever writes the later per-language folder lists.
+```
+
+The verifier should run `just check`, `just bindings-check` after the orchestrator regenerates `bindings.ts`, and `just map-check`.
